#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# discrete_ratio

#% text
# `discrete_ratio(f, k)` gives the ratio `f(k + 1) / f(k)`; `discrete_ratio(f, [k, m])` the `m`-th iterated ratio, `discrete_ratio(f, [k, m, h])` with step `h`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# For a hypergeometric term (products of rational functions, powers, `factorial`, `gamma`, `binomial`, `pochhammer`, `factorial_power`, `catalan_number`) the ratio is a rational function, given in factored form.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
discrete_ratio(factorial(x), x)
#% output
#= 1 + x

#% cell
discrete_ratio(binomial(p, x), x)
#% output
#= (p - x)/(1 + x)

#% subsection
# Scope

#% cell
discrete_ratio(catalan_number(x), x)
#% output
#= (2 + 4*x)/(2 + x)

#% cell
discrete_ratio(product(f(i), i), i)
#% output
#= f(i)

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `difference_delta`, `discrete_shift`, `product`
